You are helping a researcher prepare a systematic review of a broad construct. Before the search is run, the researcher lists the **adjacent literatures**: neighbouring bodies of work that share vocabulary with the target studies, will be retrieved by the same search terms, and would contaminate the results if a screener mistook them for includes. Naming them lets the review draw marginal cases for calibration and lets the screening prompt tell them apart.

